% This example demonstrates the specification of deontic elements, such as Obligation and Reparation. The compact serialization is used.
rule cs1:
x is a rel3 if
    x is a rel1
    and y is permitted that x is a rel2.

rule cs2:
x is a rel103 if
    x is a rel1
    and y is permitted that x is a rel2.

rule ps1:
y is forbidden that x is not a rel3 if
    the statement ps0 is violated
    and y is permitted that x is a rel1
    and y is obliged that x is a rel2
        or y is permitted that x is a rel2
    and it is not the case that the statement ps2_1 applies
    and it is not the case that the statement ps2_2 applies.

% when ps2_1 applies, the rules it overrides or attacks do not
the statement ps2_1 applies if
    the statement ps0 is violated
    and y is permitted that x is a rel1
    and y is obliged that x is a rel2
        or y is permitted that x is a rel2.

rule ps2_1:
y is forbidden that x is a rel3 if
    the statement ps2_1 applies
    and it is not the case that the statement rep1 applies
    and it is not the case that the statement rep3 applies.

% when ps2_2 applies, the rules it overrides or attacks do not
the statement ps2_2 applies if
    the statement ps0 is violated
    and y is permitted that x is a rel1
    and y is obliged that x is a rel2
        or y is permitted that x is a rel2
    and the prohibition of y that x is a rel3 is violated
    and it is not the case that the statement ps101 is violated.

rule ps2_2:
y is obliged that x is a rel4 if
    the statement ps2_2 applies.

JohnDoe is a rel5.

JaneDoe is obliged that JohnDoe is a rel5.

% when rep1 applies, the rules it overrides or attacks do not
the statement rep1 applies if
    the prohibition of y that x is not a rel3 is violated.

% reparation rep1: the penalty pen1 for a violation of ps1
rule rep1:
y is obliged that x is a rel3 if
    the statement rep1 applies
    and it is not the case that the statement ps2_1 applies.

% when rep3 applies, the rules it overrides or attacks do not
the statement rep3 applies if
    the prohibition of y that x is not a rel3 is violated.

% reparation rep3: the penalty pen1 for a violation of ps1
rule rep3:
y is obliged that x is a rel3 if
    the statement rep3 applies
    and it is not the case that the statement ps2_1 applies.

scenario permitted_and_obliged is:
    % Only the facts: nothing is violated, so ps1 and ps2 (which need a violation of ps0, a statement the document lacks) do not apply.
    x is a rel1.
    x is a rel2.
    prohibitions expects answers [].
    obligations expects answers ["JaneDoe is obliged that JohnDoe is a rel5"].
    rel103 expects answers [].
    rel3 expects answers [].
    rel5 expects answers ["JohnDoe is a rel5"].
    violated_obligations expects answers [].
    violated_prohibitions expects answers [].
    breaches expects answers [].

query prohibitions is:
    which party is forbidden that which sentence.

query obligations is:
    which party is obliged that which sentence.

query rel103 is:
    which thing is a rel103.

query rel3 is:
    which thing is a rel3.

query rel5 is:
    which thing is a rel5.

query violated_obligations is:
    the obligation of which party that which sentence is violated.

query violated_prohibitions is:
    the prohibition of which party that which sentence is violated.

query breaches is:
    which party is in breach.

